From ed6882fd623f5565085aa6dacdd709f46118ab8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:10:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: fail closed without secure IRIS1 encoder
 persist

SM8150 firmware requires encoder INTERNAL_PERSIST memory in the secure
CP_NON_PIXEL domain even for non-secure userspace sessions. The current
Venus port only has a normal DMA device on the non-secure SID.

CF7 registered PERSIST at 0xdeff0000 and reset immediately after a
successful LOAD_RESOURCES reply, before the recorded START command.
Android Q instead forces this buffer through its secure non-pixel heap
and SID.

Reject the start transaction after validating the final requirements but
before registering any internal buffer. This preserves decoder support
and prevents an unsupported encoder path from reaching the hard-reset
boundary while the secure allocator and context bank are being ported.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
index 5673f2ba4..6cef3f130 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -470,6 +470,21 @@ static int intbufs_alloc_iris1_encoder(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * SM8150 firmware requires encoder PERSIST memory in the secure
+	 * CP_NON_PIXEL domain even for a non-secure userspace session.  The
+	 * upstream Venus path has no secure allocator or context-bank device;
+	 * handing firmware a normal DMA address can hard-reset the platform
+	 * when LOAD_RESOURCES activates the encoder.  Fail before registering
+	 * any internal buffer until that complete contract is available.
+	 */
+	req = intbufs_find_req(&snapshot, HFI_BUFFER_INTERNAL_PERSIST);
+	if (req && req->size) {
+		dev_err(inst->core->dev,
+			"IRIS1 encoder requires secure CP_NON_PIXEL persist memory\n");
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Downstream calls this BUFFER_SIZE_MINIMUM; Venus names the same
 	 * 0x20100c two-u32 wire property BUFFER_SIZE_ACTUAL.  Tell firmware the
